 "what": "What NEAR testnet and Mutinynet answered for the calls ./verify.sh A makes about proofs/chrome-take.json, the take film v2 was cut from: the vault's create_vault, the thief tab's proposal, the phone page's cancel_all_and_rotate and the execute the contract refused, the three blocks the last three ran in (header times only), and the contract's account at the block of the cancel, all from archival RPC; and the take's coin from the Mutinynet API: its bytes, its status and whether it was spent. Captured 2026-11-12 UTC, when the record was proofs/film-take.json, from archival-rpc.testnet.fastnear.com and mutinynet.com. Left out, as in c14-archival.json: each answer's receipts list and its Merkle proof and metadata fields; every block field but four of its header; every account field but its code hash and block; and each transaction's signature, which the secret scan would read as a key by its length. It holds no secret: a transaction's arguments are public. tools/test/judge-floor.test.mjs serves these from stand-in nodes",
